DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261031
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261101
SUMMARY:Deadline: AI Philosophy Competition: First Edition
DESCRIPTION:The AI Philosophy Competition\, organised by philosophers Zacha
 ry Goodsell and Elliott Thornley and funded by Forethought Research\, aims
  to gauge the philosophical capabilities of AI in a way transparent to the
  philosophical community.\n\nOrganisation: Zachary Goodsell and Elliott Th
 ornley\, funded by Forethought Research\nLocation: Online submission via O
 penReview (preferred) or Google Forms\; open internationally.\nAward: USD 
 3\,000 first prize\, USD 2\,000 second\, USD 1\,000 third\, plus a USD 5\,
 000 pool for creative methodology distributed at the judges' discretion (U
 SD 11\,000 total). No entry fee.\nDuration: Finalists announced early Dece
 mber 2026\; results announced end of January 2027.\n\nMore: https://www.za
 charygoodsell.com/ai-philosophy-competition?utm_source=artificialnouveaugr
 antdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.zacharygoodsell.com/ai-philosophy-competition?utm_source=ar
 tificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Online submission via OpenReview (preferred) or Google Forms\; ope
 n internationally.
END:VEVENT
